# Expanding the Platform with Arnold & Stewart (Surface Production Operations, Vol. 1)

Arnold & Stewart is the **surface facilities** book. Cormack gave you well control, Bourgoyne gave you drilling engineering, and this book gives you the **upstream surface production system** — everything from the wellhead to custody transfer, water disposal, and crude stabilization. This is where your platform crosses from "drilling" into "production facilities." It's the natural "Phase 3" of the platform.

Your existing modules (Well Control, Drilling Hydraulics, Surface Facilities, Math Engine, Drilling Fluids, Cements, Formation, Casing, Directional, Bits, Rig Power) cover Cormack + Bourgoyne. The **Surface Facilities** module you have is minimal (pit/trip-tank). Arnold & Stewart is a **wholesale expansion** of that module plus a set of **new modules**.

---

## Module Summary: What's New vs. Expanded

| Module | Status | Priority |
|---|---|---|
| **Fluid Properties / PVT** | **NEW** — basis for everything else | v2.0 (highest) |
| **Process Selection & Flowsheet** | **NEW** — advisory/architecture | v2.0 |
| **Two-Phase Separation** | **NEW** — separator sizing engine | v2.0 (high) |
| **Three-Phase Separation** | **NEW** — FWKO, oil pad, water wash | v2.1 |
| **Pressure Vessel Design** | **NEW** — mechanical sizing, weights | v2.1 |
| **Crude Oil Treating** | **NEW** — emulsion, heater-treater, desalting | v2.1 |
| **Crude Stabilization** | **NEW** — stage separation, stabilizer | v2.2 |
| **Produced Water Treating** | **NEW** — skim, CPI, flotation, hydrocyclone | v2.1 (high) |
| **Water Injection** | **NEW** — filters, de-aeration, scavenging | v2.2 |
| **Surface Facilities** | Existing — **major expansion** (LACT, storage, drains) | v2.0 |

**The single highest-value add** is the **Fluid Properties / PVT module** — everything downstream depends on `ρ`, `Z`, `μ`, `SG`, and phase behavior. Arnold & Stewart use it in every chapter. Without it, none of the separator, treater, or water-treating equations work.

**The single biggest operational capability** is the **Two-Phase + Three-Phase Separation engine** — this is where the platform starts sizing real equipment.

**The most compelling user-facing feature** is the **Produced Water Treating** module — it turns a regulatory headache (29 mg/l, 15 mg/l, 50 mg/l depending on jurisdiction) into a defensible design calculation.

